IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-47. NOUNS of a cross-reference. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the citing words and of the target could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5755-1995, nor of any regulation made under it.
-- It records citations: for each, what the citing words say they point at, what the target is, and where each of the two readings comes from.
-- A citation whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from the citing words and from the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The Law's own words are quoted beside each value in the references modules: `ext:[r045] N |` and the other `ext:[rNNN] N |` lines are the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation of the named regulations,
-- (all of them UNOFFICIAL aids), and `ext:[SH ...]` or `ext:[KT ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument
-- (or, where the line says so, from its text layer only); each Hebrew word of such a line is checked against that page's text layer where it has one (tools/pdfcheck.py; digits, punctuation and word order are not checked by it).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

-- The schedule the citing words name by the letter B (in the pre-1995 lettering) and the schedule the Law of 1995 prints under that letter are two different schedules.
-- "The income schedule" is the schedule printed in the Law as enacted under the letter ט with [ב׳] beside it in square brackets; "the Treasury allocation schedule" is the one printed under the letter ב with [י״ד] beside it in square brackets (fork R1 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `the income schedule for the old-age pension, as a whole`
    `item 1 of the income schedule, the amount for a person without dependants`
    `item 3 of the income schedule, the amount for each further dependant`
    `the Treasury allocation schedule, as a whole`
    `item 1 of the Treasury allocation schedule, 15 percent of old-age and survivors contributions`
    `no item 3, because the Treasury allocation schedule has only items 1 and 2`

DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the consolidation, and the latest amending instrument read from its page image`
    `the consolidation, and the latest amending instrument read from its text layer only`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target if the old lettering is read as the new` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the cited item exists in the target as enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the target was repealed from` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
